 expert ratings of Solid/Safe R", "Markets price Democratic win odds near 5%"], "rationale": "The district's R+11 lean, Alfonso's decisive money advantage with heavy outside support, and a unanimous Solid/Safe R expert consensus all point to a comfortable Republican hold of Tiffany's open seat. Markets price Democratic odds near 5%, consistent with a double-digit Republican margin.", "watch": "Any late-breaking controversy around Alfonso, such as the reported voting-age comments, combined with Democratic strength in the region's traditionally blue areas, could narrow the margin.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings.", "Open seat: Tom Tiffany (R) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Tom Tiffany's retirement leaves this heavily Republican northern Wisconsin seat open, but the fundamentals still favor the GOP. The district leans Republican by about 11 points, and Republican nominee Michael Alfonso has far out-raised Democrat Fred Clark, with more than $2.2 million in outside spending boosting his campaign. Every major race rater calls the seat Solid or Safe Republican, and prediction markets give Democrats only about a 5% chance.\n\nClark, a former state legislator, has campaigned actively across the district, and some coverage notes Democratic strength in historically blue parts of the region. Alfonso has drawn some scrutiny for comments about raising the voting age and skipped a planned debate. Still, the structural Republican advantage and resource gap make an upset unlikely; the main question is the size of the winning margin.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0554, "margin": -10.68}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0396, "margin": -13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0389, "margin": -13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0525, "margin": -12.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0215, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0228, "margin": -14.0